t both paths. Interaction A11-A10-A01+A00 greater than zero suggests complementarity, but a single seed cannot establish it.',\n'Joint feedback should be more consequential on nonempty histories. For empty histories R1=R2=0 and q/w choices are functionally irrelevant at fixed parameters; this is a host correctness invariant, not an expectation of equal trained empty-slice predictions.',\n'Report all task AUC/logloss, auxiliary mean separately, and the existing predeclared history bins with sample, positive and negative counts. Other slices require authorized host availability and train-defined bins; missing diagnostics stay unavailable.',\n'Architecture cost should avoid quadratic history-history attention: readers O(B*fields*history*32), field mixing O(B*fields\"'^2*32), one linear-cost write. Report measured parameters, training/validation wall and allocated GPU seconds, examples, peak memory and model latency/throughput; no efficiency claim from FLOPs alone.'\"'\n],\n'falsifiers':[\n'If neither feedback contrast improves click AUC and A11 is within or below A00, the current feedback implementation lacks support even if every architecture beats DIN.',\n'If only one path helps, reject the need for both paths and retain the simpler supported path for follow-up. A nonpositive interaction rejects superadditivity, not all additive benefits.',\n'If padding replacement changes predictions, all-empty histories yield nonfinite results, or masking changes cause invalid gradients, the implementation fails readiness; do not interpret its predictive result.',\n'If quality gains disappear in paired seeds or require unacceptable measured cost under the fixed per-trial cap, do not claim robust improvement or efficiency. A failed single implementation does not refute all iterative interaction mechanisms.'\n],\n'alternative_explanations':[\n'DIN-to-candidate gains may come from softmax normalization, context-conditioned initial retrieval, field tokenization, raw-field skip, positio